WHY THIS LICENCE, AND HOW TO CHANGE IT

The audited tree contained no LICENCE at all (F-065). That is not a neutral
state: with nothing stated, default copyright applies but nobody can tell
whether that was intended, and a buyer, contributor or store reviewer has no
answer to "what am I allowed to do with this?".

All-rights-reserved is chosen deliberately as the reversible option. Ciyato is
being prepared for commercial release, and a permissive licence cannot be
withdrawn once published - anyone who obtained the code under it keeps those
rights forever. Starting closed preserves every choice; starting open forecloses
some of them permanently.

If the intent is open source, replacing this file is a one-line decision:

  - Apache-2.0  - permissive, includes an explicit patent grant. The usual
                  choice for a product that may later involve contributors.
  - MIT         - permissive and shorter, no patent grant.
  - GPL-3.0     - copyleft; derivative works must also be GPL. Note that this
                  is generally incompatible with distribution through the
                  Apple App Store, and imposes obligations on anyone who later
                  buys or forks the project.

Third-party dependencies carry their own licences, which are unaffected by this
file and are listed by the build's dependency report.
